{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `8a2c4cf9`, the stops of a C4 submit.\n\n1. `descriptor-mismatch` joins the union with its exact name. The\n   page learns that its package changed under a retained step. It\n   can send the live bytes again and settle. New content needs a\n   new request key.\n2. `source` joins the union with its exact name. It means that the\n   act names a source whose row the replica does not hold yet. The\n   same submit passes after the source records.\n3. The bound of 64 positions is the stop `full`, with the reason\n   `versions`. The client note, section 5.1, gives custody's stop\n   as `full` with a reason, and `signings` is one reason. A page\n   author handles one stop with one remedy in each case: this key\n   takes no more, so the member continues with a new request key.\n   The reason says which bound. `AuthorizationError` keeps\n   `versions-full` inside the client.\n   If the public stop of C3 does not carry custody's reason, or if\n   a reason of `full` has another remedy than a new key or a wait\n   for a closed signing, tell me and keep `versions-full` as its\n   own stop.\n4. `authorization-used` stays internal, as you say.\n5. The how-to page of C4 has one table: each stop, what it means,\n   and what the page does next. Nine rows.\n\nI add the mapping to the next amendment of the act environment\nnote, section 15.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}